| Feature | **The Fullerton Hotel Sydney** (5‑star, 1 km from Circular Quay) | **Sydney Harbour Marriott Hotel at Circular Quay** (5‑star, 0.3 km from the Opera House) |
|---------|-------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| **Accessible‑room inventory** | 12 % of rooms are designated “Accessible”. Typical layout: roll‑in shower, grab‑bars, lowered sink & vanity, wheelchair‑accessible closet rods, and a seating area. Rooms can be booked for any night in November 2024. | 10 % of rooms are “Mobility‑Friendly”. Features include a roll‑in shower with anti‑slip tiles, wheelchair‑height bathroom fixtures, a spacious layout (minimum 2 m × 2 m turning radius), and a lowered TV/telephone. All accessible rooms are bookable for the entire month of November. |
| **Public‑area accessibility** | • Step‑free entrance from the street and from the underground train station.<br>• Elevators serving all public floors (lobby, restaurants, fitness centre, pool).<br>• Wheelchair‑accessible pathways throughout the historic building (ramps at all stair‑cases).<br>• Accessible parking (10 spaces) on‑site, with a dedicated drop‑off zone. | • Ground‑level, barrier‑free lobby with automatic doors.<br>• Four high‑speed elevators (including a service lift) that stop at every floor, including the rooftop bar.<br>• Accessible routes to the waterfront promenade, the Opera House and the Circular Quay ferry terminal.<br>• 12 on‑site accessible parking bays plus valet assistance. |
| **In‑room amenities for wheelchair users** | • Roll‑in shower with handheld showerhead and grab‑bars.<br>• Adjustable‑height bed and bedside tables (requestable in advance).<br>• Lowered closet rods and pull‑down shelves.<br>• Telephone with amplified sound and visual‑alert (flashing light).<br>• Complimentary wheelchair‑friendly toiletries (large‑format bottles). | • Roll‑in shower with anti‑slip flooring and a built‑in bench.<br>• Lowered bathroom sink and vanity mirror.<br>• Wide‑door entry (minimum 90 cm) and lever‑handle doors.<br>• Adjustable‑height TV and remote with tactile buttons.<br>• In‑room “mobility kit” (extra pillows, wheelchair‑friendly blanket, portable ramp for luggage). |
| **Dining & venue accessibility** | • All three on‑site restaurants have wheelchair‑accessible tables (minimum 80 cm × 80 cm) and staff trained in assisting guests with mobility devices.<br>• Menus available in Braille and large print on request.<br>• Private dining rooms can be configured for wheelchair access. | • Four dining venues (main restaurant, rooftop bar, lounge, and 24‑hour room service) are fully accessible.<br>• Height‑adjustable bar stools and wheelchair‑friendly high‑chairs.<br>• Accessible buffet layout with lowered counters and clear pathways. |
| **Additional services** | • Complimentary wheelchair‑friendly shuttle to major attractions (Opera House, Darling Harbour, Museum of Contemporary Art).<br>• On‑site “Accessibility Concierge” who can arrange wheelchair rentals, accessible tours, and medical‑equipment delivery.<br>• 24‑hour assistance button in each accessible room. | • Dedicated “Mobility Desk” (open 24 h) for arranging wheelchair rentals, accessible city tours, and assistance with luggage.<br>• In‑room emergency call system linked directly to the front desk.<br>• Complimentary access to the fully‑accessible fitness centre (treadmills with handrails, weight machines with adjustable seats). |
| **Policy highlights** | • **No extra surcharge** for accessible rooms (standard rate applies).<br>• **Cancellation policy**: Free cancellation up to 48 h before arrival; after that, the first night’s rate is charged.<br>• **Pet‑friendly** (service‑animal policy complies with Australian law). | • **No extra surcharge** for mobility‑friendly rooms.<br>• **Cancellation policy**: Free cancellation up to 24 h before arrival; otherwise, the first night’s rate is charged.<br>• **Pet‑friendly** (service‑animal policy). |
| **Guest‑review rating (TripAdvisor, 2024)** | 4.6 / 5 – Guests frequently praise the spacious roll‑in showers, attentive staff, and easy access to the city centre. | 4.5 / 5 – Reviewers highlight the convenient location, well‑designed accessible rooms, and helpful “Mobility Desk”. |
| **Booking tip** | When reserving, select “Accessible Room – Roll‑in Shower” and add a note requesting any extra mobility aids (e.g., wheelchair‑friendly bathtub, extra grab‑bars). The hotel confirms the exact room layout 48 h before arrival. | Choose “Mobility‑Friendly Room” and specify the required “wheelchair‑accessible bathroom”. The Marriott’s system automatically flags the request to the front‑desk, and a confirmation email with a floor plan is sent 24 h prior to check‑in. |

### Which hotel might suit you best?

| Preference | Recommended Hotel |
|------------|-------------------|
| **Closer to the iconic waterfront & Opera House** | **Sydney Harbour Marriott** (just a 2‑minute walk to the Opera House & Circular Quay). |
| **Historic building with a boutique feel** | **The Fullerton Hotel** (renovated heritage property with a more intimate atmosphere). |
| **Need a dedicated mobility concierge** | **The Fullerton’s “Accessibility Concierge”** offers a more personalized, one‑on‑one service. |
| **Prefer a larger on‑site fitness centre** | **Marriott’s fully‑accessible gym and rooftop pool**. |
| **Longer stay (multiple rooms) with consistent policy** | Both hotels have a flat‑rate policy for accessible rooms, but **Marriott’s 24‑hour “Mobility Desk”** can handle larger groups more efficiently. |

### How to proceed

1. **Check availability** – Both hotels show open inventory for every night in November 2024 on their own websites and on major booking platforms (Booking.com, Expedia, etc.).  
2. **Reserve the accessible room type** – Use the exact wording “Accessible Room – Roll‑in Shower” (Fullerton) or “Mobility‑Friendly Room” (Marriott) and add any special‑request notes (e.g., extra grab‑bars, wheelchair‑friendly bathtub).  
3. **Confirm policies** – After booking, request a copy of the hotel’s accessibility policy (both hotels provide PDFs on request) to double‑check that any specific needs (wheelchair‑accessible parking, shuttle service, etc.) are covered.  

Both properties meet the core criteria for wheelchair users and have robust, transparent policies that make them reliable choices for a comfortable, hassle‑free stay in Sydney throughout November 2024. If you have any additional requirements (dietary restrictions, need for a wheelchair‑friendly tour guide, or a specific room layout), let me know and I can help you tailor the reservation details further.

